
CURTEST - one cursor, or two?
  the BIOS moves it, DOS writes:
    OK   the character landed where the BIOS left the cursor
    OK   and the BIOS can see where DOS left it
  and alternating, on one line:
    OK   INT 10h then INT 21h wrote YZ, side by side
    OK   and both of them moved the cursor on
  and DOS moves it, the BIOS reads it back:
    OK   the same position, both ways round
CURTEST done
